{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_k3rlte7sw6ya24gtwkltz3b7mzyxnivhgosj62jz5u2xufs3vmnq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **all four phases pass, and one real translation bug was found and fixed.**\n\n## The bug: NaN payload propagation\n\nThe Rust translation diverged from C on **7 of the 29 low-level configuration rows**. Root cause: the C library compiles to x86-64 SSE scalar instructions (`mulss`/`addss`/`subss`/`divss`), which propagate NaN operands **asymmetrically** — the *destination* register's payload wins. Which C operand GCC puts in the destination is **not always the left-hand one**:\n\n| C source | emitted | dst |\n|---|---|---|\n| `a.x += b.x` (`c2Add`) | `addss %xmm1(a.x),%xmm0(b.x)` | `b.x` ← **right** |\n| `a.x*b.x + a.y*b.y` (`c2Dot`) | 2nd `mulss %xmm2(a.y),%xmm0(b.y)` | `b.y` ← **right** |\n| `out->t = t0 * A.t` | `mulss t0,%xmm0(A.t)` | `A.t` ← **right** |\n| `yAp.y + (…)*t` | `addss %xmm1(yAp.y),%xmm0(prod)` | product ← **right** |\n\nThe original Rust used plain `f32` operators, so LLVM freely commuted them and the wrong operand's payload survived. Fix: added `fmul`/`fadd`/`fsub`/`fdiv` helpers implementing exact SSE NaN priority, and wired each of the ~30 call sites with the `(dst, src)` order read off the C disassembly.\n\nTwo other test-side issues were mine, not the translation's: naive ULP-boundary construction (`bits-1` on negatives), and a debug-only divergence where `-C debug-assertions` turns a NULL write into SIGABRT instead of C's SIGSEGV — the shipping `--release` cdylib segfaults identically.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 22/22 symbols, `comm -23` empty, `ldd -r` clean. No module was skipped, no stubs.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 51 rows, one per distinct rejection branch, all covered by a passing test.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 68 rows across the option axis (`C2_TYPE` dispatch), value classes, ABI classes (20-byte MEMORY structs), and geometric branches.\n- `tests/` — 114 test functions loading **both** `.so`s via `libloading`, comparing return values *and* full out-struct bit patterns (`to_bits`), with a `SENTINEL` so \"did the callee write `*out`?\" is itself compared.\n- `verify_all.sh` — Phase D driver: 3 feature combos × 2 profiles = 6 configurations, all green.\n\n## Results\n\n- Zero divergences over **~60M randomized calls** at `DIFF_SCALE=120`, including ±0, denormals, ±inf, signalling NaNs, and raw random bit patterns.\n- Out-of-range `C2_TYPE` values (`3`, `-1`, `INT_MAX`, `INT_MIN`, …) verified: the C `switch` has no `default` and falls off the end, so the return value is genuinely indeterminate. The test asserts the only well-defined property — neither library writes `*out` — rather than pretending to compare UB.\n- No binary/driver exists (`CMakeLists.txt` only does `add_library(... SHARED ...)`), so the stdout gate is N/A — asserted mechanically in the script.\n- `c_src/` unmodified (321/12/17 lines, original timestamps)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":204284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":546,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fe3e95-e99c-4c8e-a206-30b9bab42fd1","uuid":"1459d181-0ccc-4c48-ac60-9061a4b89efc","timestamp":"2026-09-05T12:09:40.833Z"}
